    "posts": [
      {
        "id": "post-pipeline-to-tt",
        "slug": "from-pipeline-punch-to-tropical-trouble",
        "status": "published",
        "data": {
          "title": "From Pipeline Punch to Tropical Trouble: Lowering the Barrier to 3lb Combat Robotics",
          "excerpt": "How we turned our MRCA Championship & NHRL Top-8 beetleweight architecture into an accessible, 100% 3D-printable combat robot kit.",
          "featured_image": "/products/tt-kit-1.jpg",
          "content": [
            {
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "When I set out to design the Tropical Trouble 3lb beetleweight kit, the goal was simple: take the lessons learned from winning the 2024 MRCA Championship with Pipeline Punch and placing in the Top 8 at NHRL, and package them into a fully 3D-printable platform that any builder can maintain on a $180 Bambu Lab A1 Mini.",
                  "_key": "k_f9p8xw1"
                }
              ],
              "_key": "b_avvdw5y"
            },
            {
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Why 100% 3D-Printed Construction?",
                  "_key": "k_bwa2x5c"
                }
              ],
              "_key": "b_4w0tjkq"
            },
            {
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Traditional billet aluminum or carbon-fiber beetleweight kits are expensive to machine and punishing when a spare frame rail gets bent mid-tournament. By designing Tropical Trouble around a multi-zone TPU chassis with cast 45A Vytaflex urethane wheels and a 6\" Repeat Robotics 2812 hubmotor spinner (217 MPH tip speed), builders can print replacement chassis, uprights, wheel guards, and forks overnight before an event.",
                  "_key": "k_c5myj6c"
                }
              ],
              "_key": "b_4timawm"
            },
            {
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Engineering Calculator Suite",
                  "_key": "k_2ai6ofh"
                }
              ],
              "_key": "b_qduh4i7"
            },
            {
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Before modifying weapon diameters, pulley ratios, or LiHV cell counts, make sure to test your configuration in our native LNCR Combat Robotics Engineering Calculator Suite!",
                  "_key": "k_x7088b7"
                }
              ],
              "_key": "b_qtli81e"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    ],
